WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.600
[Bass hit]
Your Hermes Desktop. In a tab.

2
00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:03.200
127.0.0.1:9120
Countdown: 1:00 until the link dies

3
00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:05.500
[Typing] 1/3 Turn it on.
hermes config set webapp.enabled true

4
00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:08.400
[Typing] 2/3 Restart the gateway.
hermes gateway restart

5
00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:10.800
[Typing] 3/3 Get the link.
hermes webapp

6
00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:13.300
[Bass hit]
Your whole Desktop.

7
00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:15.800
The app opens in a browser tab
at 127.0.0.1:9120.

8
00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:20.800
[Click]
Messaging setup.

9
00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:25.400
[Bass hit]
Skills. Plugins. Tools.

10
00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:30.800
[Click]
Scheduled jobs.

11
00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:35.400
[Bass hit]
Every setting.

12
00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:40.800
[Click]
One gateway. One chat queue.

13
00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:43.000
[Bass hit]
Stays in the desktop app:

14
00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:46.800
1. Global shortcuts 2. Always-on-top
overlays 3. The updater (Hermes docs)

15
00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:50.800
Sign in to Hermes
A fresh tab can't get in.

16
00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:53.500
[Bass hit]
One link. One use.

17
00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:56.000
[Clock ticking]
127.0.0.1:9120/webapp/launch#ticket=…

18
00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:58.400
[Ticking] Same link, second use: the page
says it was already used or has expired.

19
00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:00.900
[Ticking] It says to run hermes webapp
again for a new one.

20
00:01:00.900 --> 00:01:03.600
[Bass hit]
Expired. One use. 60 seconds.

21
00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:05.400
[Two bass hits]
A red lock appears.

22
00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:07.400
This tab can run any command as you.
Keep it local. webapp.host: 127.0.0.1

23
00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:10.000
Try it on canary. Copy this:
hermes config set webapp.enabled true

24
00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:12.800
hermes gateway restart · hermes webapp
Or paste the safety check into Hermes.

25
00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:15.500
Main / canary only. Not in stable yet.
PR #141864 · port 9120
